    "standardized_narrative": "Using the gross claims development triangle the Syndicate experienced a net gross prior-year adverse development of approximately GBP 16.6m (5.3% of opening gross claims reserves), driven largely by adverse development on recent long-tail US casualty years (notably 2021-2022) and increases in large loss development. Offsetting releases occurred in some property years, but the aggregate gross movement is a strengthening of reserves. The Managing Agent cites latent claims emergence and litigation funding/social inflation as key drivers and notes several named catastrophe events (Hurricane Ian 2022, Maui fires 2023, Los Angeles wildfires 2024) that affected loss experience.",
